// A PARITY WITNESS, not a floor: with the annotation present there is nothing to
// infer, so the count is the reader's problem and both compilers say so - and they
// said so before this change too.
//
// It is here because the change moved the order of two questions and this shape
// answers the second one; no perturbation I tried reddens it, which is stated
// rather than dressed up. The floor for the CHOICE is the accept-side fixture
// c71, where refusing to infer turns a legal program away.
enum E<T> { P(T) | Q }
fn main() {
    let e: E<int> = E::P(1, 2);
    println(1);
}
